                    load_sequenced:         `Two levers, sequenced — pick the two that change behaviour before the customer visit and embed them`,
                    load_overload:          `All of them in week one — delegation, voice channels, recognition, new huddles, on top of the day job`,
                    load_one:               `A single lever only — safe, but too little to move the floor in eight weeks`,
                    lever_delegation:       `Delegation — push line-stop authority for quality down to the worker who sees the defect`,
                    lever_voice:            `Voice — daily huddles & a no-blame escape-reporting channel so problems surface early`,
                    lever_recognition:      `Recognition — visibly reward workers who surface problems and own the right local call`,
                    frame_care:             `As paternalist care — “the firm trusts and protects you to stop a bad part” — voice WITHIN respected hierarchy`,
                    frame_mandate:          `As a top-down mandate — order the huddles and audit attendance hard`,
                    frame_western:          `As a Western flat model — “no more bosses, everyone is equal now”`,

                    r3_incident_label:      `A worker used line-stop authority over a minor issue (2-hour stoppage). The veteran Operations Lead demands you revoke it. Your move?`,
                    r3_veteran_label:       `The veteran Operations Lead runs 40% of the floor and distrusts "empowerment." How do you handle him?`,
                    r3_visit_label:         `The German customer wants a plant visit in two weeks. What do you show them?`,
                    r3_protect_label:       `Protect frontline time & coaching so supervisors can actually embed the change? (%)`,
                    r3_protect_readout:     `Backfill & supervisor coaching time:`,
                    inc_reinforce:          `Reinforce the authority publicly — thank the worker for stopping, treat the false alarm as the cost of learning`,
                    inc_retract:            `Retract line-stop authority — restore order, the two-hour stoppage was too expensive`,
                    inc_quiet:              `Keep it on paper but quietly discourage its use until things settle`,
                    vet_owner:              `Make him an owner — give him a visible role designing the line-stop rules, honour his authority and experience`,
                    vet_overrule:           `Overrule him publicly — make an example so the floor knows you're serious`,
                    vet_bypass:             `Bypass him — work directly with his team and route around his resistance`,
                    visit_progress:         `Honest early behaviours — the huddles, the first escapes caught, plus a credible 90-day plan; no overclaiming`,
                    visit_transformed:      `Declare the culture “transformed” — show a polished launch event and confident metrics`,
                    visit_hide:             `Delay or stage the visit — show only the best line and avoid the night shift`,

