                    insight_embedded:       `Empowerment that lasts: you raised voice, delegation and recognition WHILE honouring hürmet and paternalist care — the Empowerment Index is on a credible trajectory, Cultural-Fit held, engagement and quality climbed together. Hierarchy and voice now coexist.`,
                    insight_norespect:      `You raised the Empowerment Index but Cultural-Fit fell below the floor — you imposed empowerment instead of adapting it. The veteran lines read it as dishonour, and an empowerment that the middle layer resents won't survive.`,
                    insight_thin:           `The Empowerment Index hit the target but engagement or quality stayed thin — the behaviours haven't truly taken root, and the change is fragile.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the ≥70 Empowerment Index the board needs to credibly defend to the customer. Re-examine which lever you under-played — most likely voice, the imperfect-first-use test, or the veteran supervisor.`,
                    insight_fitfloor:       `Cultural-Fit dropped below 50 — somewhere you dishonoured local norms (a flat model, a Western frame, or overruling the veteran). In a high-power-distance context that provokes resistance that quietly undoes the change.`,
                    insight_voicekilled:    `You taught the floor that speaking up is unsafe — by retracting delegated authority or mandating compliance. That single signal can undo months of empowerment work.`,
